  "body": "Found while working #904 (pinning the containment solid law on a reduced-fidelity model). This is in the code PR #911 merged; #904's slice does not change it.\n\n**What happens.** A drill matched to its hole, on a model flagged between about 0.0105 mm and 0.015 mm (the refusal bound), is convicted with `Gouge` at its first plunge, even when it stops well above the hole's floor. The gate then blocks the post with a gouge that is not there. Below about 0.0105 mm (a metre-unit file's 0.01 mm included) and at full fidelity it is clean.\n\n**Repro.** A 40 x 40 x 20 block with a 20 x 20 blind hole to Z 10, a 4 mm drill (`DR-0400`), one `Hole { radius: 2.0, entry_z: 20.0, floor_z: 10.0 }`, Bottom Z 10.2:\n\n| model imported at | blocking warnings |\n|---|---|\n| full fidelity, 0.008 ... 0.0105 mm | none |\n| 0.011 mm, 0.012 mm, 0.0149 mm | `Gouge { at: 1 }` |\n| 0.03 mm (refused by name at the gate) | none |\n\n(`crates/app/tests/coarse_contain.rs` on #904's branch has the fixture; pass `Some(0.011)` and a bottom of 10.2.)\n\n**Likely cause.** The section law (b) reads `floor = r - leave - cx.tightened(cx.gouge_tol)` (`sim` `verify/section.rs`). `GOUGE_TOL` exists to absorb the chord error of our own regions (`operation/material.rs`: \"half the geo2d round-join chord error plus room for float chains\"). A drill's region is the hole's rim as a polygon, so a matched drill's centre stands a few microns inside `r` by construction. Once the model's excess has taken more than about half the tolerance, what is left no longer covers that polygon's own sagitta, and the law convicts the drill against its own rim. The same may hold for other kinds whose regions carry our own chords (bore, thread mill, circular).\n\n**What is owed.** Decide how law (b) should split its tolerance between our own discretization and the model's excess (for example: tighten only the part of the tolerance not spent on the region's own chord error, or build these rims finer), so an honest drill is not convicted on a model that is still judged.\n\n**Done means:** a matched drill, bore and thread mill on a model flagged anywhere below the refusal bound verify clean, with a pin at 0.0149 mm; a real gouge there is still convicted.\n",
